      "body": "North's fulfillment appliance is deployed independently of this service. Operations handoff F-17 reports that it accepts only CSV v1 with fields id,sku,quantity and cannot ingest JSONL v2. South and newly onboarded sites accept JSONL v2. Shipping this service does not upgrade north's receiver.\n\nPreserve north's CSV routing until Operations confirms its receiver migration. Do not infer receiver capability from local encoder support, service releases, or passing tests. JSONL v2 is compatible with the reported south/new-site deployments; this is not a mandate to change their routing.\n\nIncident F-18 reports that normal deliveries and disaster-recovery replacements terminate at the same ingestion gateway and are polled by the same north appliance. Changes to this receiver contract require review of both export paths, even though they have different service entry points.\n\nEvidence is reported by Operations (F-17 and F-18), not independently verified by repository tests. Code anchors identify affected code at the inspected baseline, not evidence of deployment. Reassess this constraint when Operations confirms migration or reports a changed site capability or gateway topology; update both dependent export decisions then.",
