      "body": "Disaster-recovery replacements are another delivery to the same north receiver, not a separate compatibility domain. Apply the linked receiver contract to recovery format selection, including when changing recovery independently of normal exports. Review both paths whenever the receiver contract changes.\n\nWhile preserving compatible output, recovery must continue reconstructing the latest shipment image with latest-upsert/delete semantics. A format migration must not replace that reconstruction with an export of raw historical events or otherwise resurrect deleted shipments. This is a required behavior from F-18; the implementation of replay_events itself does not warrant a separate knowledge node.\n\nThe cross-path receiver obligation is reported in Operations incident F-18 and grounded in F-17's deployment constraint. Local tests exercise latest upsert and deletion and explicit encoding, but cannot verify that the deployed appliance polls both paths or has migrated. Code anchors locate the affected recovery entry point only.\n\nReassess compatibility when Operations changes the receiver contract or reports a different recovery destination. Changes to reconstruction semantics require a separate explicit requirement; receiver migration alone does not invalidate latest-upsert/delete behavior.",
